WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.110
"I've found my champion." Hermes peered through the crack in the temple wall. "Finish creating the passage, my friend."

2
00:00:15.111 --> 00:00:22.474
"Are you certain?" Caerus sounded bored. "These time passages aren't a simple matter, you know.

3
00:00:22.475 --> 00:00:25.494
None of the other gods could even begin to—"

4
00:00:25.495 --> 00:00:28.351
"I know," Hermes interrupted.

5
00:00:28.352 --> 00:00:31.263
"That's why I asked you to help me. Trust me.

6
00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:36.014
It will be worth the effort if we succeed." He smiled.

7
00:00:36.015 --> 00:00:43.616
Caerus smiled back, looking more interested now. "True," he said.

8
00:00:43.617 --> 00:00:48.329
"Zeus will never figure out where you found your champion!"

9
00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:54.041
Hermes didn't respond. He was watching the mortal boy again.

10
00:00:54.042 --> 00:00:59.798
It wasn't easy to see through the tiny crack in the wall—curse Caerus and his laziness!

11
00:00:59.799 --> 00:01:07.951
But Hermes could see enough. The athlete was handsome and strong, his muscles rippling as he ran. Other

12
00:01:07.952 --> 00:01:12.447
mortals were chasing the boy, but he outpaced them easily. Suddenly

13
00:01:12.448 --> 00:01:19.631
the boy stopped. He threw something on the ground and then leaped around gracefully. "Is

14
00:01:19.632 --> 00:01:26.788
he celebrating his victory in the footrace?" Hermes thought. Watching him, Hermes had no idea. The

15
00:01:26.789 --> 00:01:32.053
ways of mortals were often strange, and usually not worth puzzling over. But

16
00:01:32.054 --> 00:01:37.254
Hermes could tell that this mortal was something special. "Finish

17
00:01:37.255 --> 00:01:50.395
the passage," he told Caerus again. "We don't have time to waste if we want to have him ready." *

18
00:01:50.396 --> 00:01:57.245
* * "Good game, Brody," Coach Smith said as Brody jogged off the field with the rest of the

19
00:01:57.246 --> 00:02:05.186
football team. "Yeah, I know." Brody puffed out his chest. "Thanks, Coach. Do you think we'll win the championship

20
00:02:05.187 --> 00:02:13.002
this year?" Another player glanced over. "If you keep making touchdowns, Brody? Definitely!"

21
00:02:13.003 --> 00:02:20.648
he said. Several of Brody's other teammates agreed, though some remained quiet. A few

22
00:02:20.649 --> 00:02:27.973
looked unhappy. Brody wasn't surprised. He was only a freshman, but he played better than any of the

23
00:02:27.974 --> 00:02:32.551
older kids. That had to be embarrassing for them. Brody didn't

24
00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:37.140
care, though. They should be glad he was on

25
00:02:37.141 --> 00:02:41.894
the team. Everyone said he was the best player to attend the high school

26
00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:44.906
in years. Maybe he was the best

27
00:02:44.907 --> 00:02:53.459
player ever. Brody headed into the locker room. He showered, changed his clothes, and went

28
00:02:53.460 --> 00:03:00.759
back outside. A teammate waved good-bye. "Are you ready for that science test tomorrow?" he

29
00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:06.459
called. Brody frowned at him. "Who cares about

30
00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:10.132
science?" The truth was, he hadn't studied for the test

31
00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:15.375
yet. Science was hard for him—even harder than most of his other

32
00:03:15.376 --> 00:03:22.185
classes. But so what? The coach was already saying that Brody was sure to win a college scholarship when the time

33
00:03:22.186 --> 00:03:28.600
came. Brody didn't care much about going to college, but he loved the idea of playing college

34
00:03:28.601 --> 00:03:33.277
football. After that he'd probably be drafted by the professional league, and then he'd be

35
00:03:33.278 --> 00:03:36.665
rich. He wouldn't need to know about science to play

36
00:03:36.666 --> 00:03:40.952
football. The only schooling he'd need was enough math to add up all his

37
00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:44.875
money! As Brody was thinking about that, a girl stepped in front of

38
00:03:44.876 --> 00:03:48.678
him. He almost crashed into her, but he stopped just in

39
00:03:48.679 --> 00:03:54.069
time. "Watch it," he said. "I'm trying to walk

40
00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:59.057
here." "I need to talk to you." The girl sounded

41
00:03:59.058 --> 00:04:05.343
annoyed. Brody stared at her. She looked familiar. "Hey, don't you ride my

42
00:04:05.344 --> 00:04:11.408
bus?" "Yes." The girl sounded even more annoyed now. "I sit in the front

43
00:04:11.409 --> 00:04:16.190
seat. Every single day since school started. I'm

44
00:04:16.191 --> 00:04:19.162
Julia." "Oh. Uh, I'm

45
00:04:19.163 --> 00:04:27.476
Brody." "I know." Julia rolled her eyes. "I'm supposed to write an article about you for the school

46
00:04:27.477 --> 00:04:32.700
newspaper." "Really?" Brody shrugged. "There was an article about me in there three weeks

47
00:04:32.701 --> 00:04:38.554
ago. I guess it's time for another one." He laughed

48
00:04:38.555 --> 00:04:44.247
loudly. Julia didn't laugh. "Just so you know, I don't care about

49
00:04:44.248 --> 00:04:50.250
football. They're making me do this because the reporter who usually writes the sports stories is sick."

50
00:04:50.251 --> 00:04:55.148
"Whatever." Brody started walking. "I'm on my way to the bus stop.

51
00:04:55.149 --> 00:04:58.094
You can interview me if you can keep up."

52
00:04:58.095 --> 00:05:05.036
Julia broke into a jog to match his pace. "Can't you hold still for a second?

53
00:05:05.037 --> 00:05:09.573
This won't take long." She looked at her notebook.

54
00:05:09.574 --> 00:05:14.055
"What's your favorite thing about playing on the football team?"

55
00:05:14.056 --> 00:05:19.184
That got Brody's interest. He loved talking about himself.

56
00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:23.580
He stopped and leaned against the brick wall of the gymnasium.

57
00:05:23.581 --> 00:05:29.686
"Well . . . ," he said. "My favorite thing about playing football is that I'm so great at it.

58
00:05:29.687 --> 00:05:36.374
It's fun being the star of the team." He flexed his biceps like a bodybuilder.

59
00:05:36.375 --> 00:05:43.852
"Hmm." Julia didn't look impressed by that, or by his answer either, but she scribbled a few notes.

60
00:05:43.853 --> 00:05:48.316
"What valuable lessons have you learned from your teammates so far?"

61
00:05:48.317 --> 00:05:52.952
That question wasn't nearly as interesting as the first one, in Brody's opinion.

62
00:05:52.953 --> 00:05:57.070
"What kind of article are you writing, anyway?" he said.

63
00:05:57.071 --> 00:05:59.216
"Readers won't care about stuff like that.

64
00:05:59.217 --> 00:06:03.742
Maybe you should wait until that sick reporter gets back and let him write the story."

65
00:06:03.743 --> 00:06:08.885
He started to walk away. Then he felt Julia grab his arm.

66
00:06:08.886 --> 00:06:11.917
She had a strong grip for such a nerdy girl.

67
00:06:11.918 --> 00:06:17.890
"Stop," she said, sounding annoyed. "I told you, I need to—"

68
00:06:17.891 --> 00:06:19.147
Whoosh!

69
00:06:19.148 --> 00:06:22.612
. A sudden blast of air and sound interrupted

70
00:06:22.613 --> 00:06:26.126
her. The bricks of the gym wall seemed to crackle and melt.

71
00:06:26.127 --> 00:06:32.538
They pulled apart, leaving a narrow opening just tall and wide enough for a person to step through.

72
00:06:32.539 --> 00:06:35.430
Brody felt Julia's grip on him tighten.

73
00:06:35.431 --> 00:06:39.740
As he looked through the crack, his eyes widened in shock.

74
00:06:39.741 --> 00:06:44.418
There was no sign of the gym interior through that crack in the wall.

75
00:06:44.419 --> 00:06:52.611
Instead he saw a strange, shadowy space with stone walls. Two tall figures stood there.

76
00:06:52.612 --> 00:06:55.636
One of the figures leaned through the crack.

77
00:06:55.637 --> 00:07:04.430
He had curly blond hair and looked a few years older than Brody. His eyes glowed bright green.

78
00:07:04.431 --> 00:07:16.591
"Hey . . . Ow!" Brody yelped as the mysterious figure grabbed him by the hair and yanked him through the crack.

